#====================================================================
# Draft: toybox diff has no -e (ed script) mode — consumers of
#        `diff -e` (changetrack, recon/restore tooling) need GNU
#        diffutils ahead of toybox on PATH
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-TOYBOX-DIFF-E-ED-SCRIPT
trigger_tool:           toybox|diff|-e|ed|diffutils|changetrack|GNU diff
phase:                  testing|runtime-environment
error_signature:        Unknown option 'e'|Can't do diff -e|diff: Unknown option

severity:               2
category:               platform-userland-gap
match_keywords:         toybox, diff, diff -e, ed script, diffutils, changetrack, PATH, userland, silent empty ed script

title:                  toybox diff 缺 -e（ed 脚本）输出，核心路径依赖 `diff -e` 的脚本必须让 GNU diffutils 先于 toybox 出现在 PATH

root_cause:             toybox (0.8.12) diff implements -u/-c style output only; `-e` (ed editor commands, required for replayable edit scripts) is unsupported. Failure point is a SILENT EMPTY ed script, not a crash: a consumer that resolves `diff` from ambient PATH gets toybox (/usr/bin/diff), `diff -e` prints "diff: Unknown option 'e'" to stderr, exits rc=2 with EMPTY stdout. changetrack 4.7 opens `diff -e "$yestfile" "$realfile"` as a pipe (changetrack source line 341); open() succeeds, so it collects an empty @ed and writes an empty `.ed` restore file — the recovery path is silently corrupted while the change log still records the edit. `die "Can't do diff -e:$!"` fires only when diff cannot be executed at all. Device default PATH resolves /usr/bin (toybox) before the toolchain userland dir carrying GNU diffutils 3.10.
affected_scope:         Any script/tool piping `diff -e` (changetrack 4.7 verified; typical of config-monitor/restore tooling; same exposure for future `diff --ed` / `patch -e` consumers). Unaffected: plain `diff`/`diff -u` consumers (toybox supports those).
verification_cmd:       printf 'a\nb\nc\n' > o; printf 'a\nX\nc\n' > n; diff -e o n   (ambient=toybox: "diff: Unknown option 'e'", rc=2, stdout empty); PATH=/data/service/hnp/bin:$PATH diff -e o n   (GNU diffutils 3.10: prints "2c"/"X"/".", rc=1) — PATH precedence alone fixes it

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           path-precedence-for-gnu-diffutils
rec_description:        Ensure the runtime PATH puts the GNU userland dir (which provides GNU diffutils 3.10, archives/d/diffutils) before /usr/bin when executing such consumers; in Conan test_packages run under the profile buildenv (env="conanbuild") whose PATH already prepends that dir. In tests, assert on the ed-script content (e.g. contains the hunk header "2c") so shadowing by toybox fails loudly instead of silently. Design rationale: prefer PATH precedence over patching the consumer (patching only as fallback); trust behavioral evidence over assumptions (content assertions, not exit codes); keep delivered files relocatable (see forbid_1).
rec_command:            conan create archives/c/changetrack/4.7 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               CI profile ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 [buildenv] PATH (already correct); test_package/conanfile.py of archives/c/changetrack/4.7 for the assertion pattern

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      patch-consumer-to-inject-diff-args
fallback_description:   If PATH control is impossible, patch the consumer to invoke an explicit diff implementation or degrade to supported modes (e.g. changetrack -u for unified diffs in human logs), while keeping `diff -e` only behind an availability check. Aligns with P013: degrade on platform limits instead of bypassing.
fallback_command:       grep -n "diff -e" <consumer-script>
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       hardcode the device-absolute diffutils path inside delivered recipes|replace system toybox|ship a bundled diff binary in the package
forbid_1_reason:        Delivered files must stay relocatable (no private absolute paths); mutating system userland or bundling shadow binaries creates system collisions (R26) and breaks other consumers.
forbid_1_consequence:   Non-relocatable recipes, L5/R26 warnings, or a broken device userland.

# Layer 4: Principles
principles:             P013

# Relations
similar_to:             [E402,E010,E098]

related:
    - archives/d/diffutils (3.10, GNU diffutils, provides diff -e)
    - archives/c/changetrack/4.7 (verified consumer)

# Metadata
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-toybox-diff-e-ed-script.md
